{"card_hash": "60d0138e18b65a9525cf9a4a99f2514e38aed7ba9f82f84a15efccefae4d5303", "channel": "Practical AI", "chars": 37332, "chars_all_clips": 37332, "chars_chosen_clips": 1440, "clip_count": 41, "clips": [{"deep_link": "https://share.transistor.fm/s/9d74230b#t=1", "end": 75.865005, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "00d1f64b9e50371a6803968ceffc8af49777037930ad3b5d22b0df5dc16af29b", "start": 1.76, "text": "Welcome to the Practical AI Podcast, where we break down the real world applications of artificial intelligence and how it's shaping the way we live, work, and create. Our goal is to help make AI technology practical, productive, and access", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://share.transistor.fm/s/9d74230b#t=768", "end": 854.085, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "34b280631d8b09f8d5f0d90fc11fdf964e8d2a79a7ae5f84e76639367541e9f7", "start": 768.55505, "text": "It could access services reachable from the proxy's network. So this is kind of working through that that software installation or proxy package proxy. It could read configuration, credentials, and allow the proxy to relay otherwise blocked", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://share.transistor.fm/s/9d74230b#t=922", "end": 990.485, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "5dd3b1bf3e4f9492aa123ed99a61add32911171872c7d87e2e418d69f04ae378", "start": 922.23, "text": "Right? How and all the time here at our like, this has been a big topic for us, internally as a company. How are we doing this sandboxing? How are we protecting ourselves, but also creating a product that allows other people to do this? And", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://share.transistor.fm/s/9d74230b#t=1439", "end": 1534.35, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "815e0f6efafa10a7c5ee5d5982511b698fff88e70fa967e5f38365102ee3e4d6", "start": 1439.2051, "text": "That's just a reminder maybe to folks out there, like, before you download Hugging Face repositories, you might wanna check the source and check the security scans, have your own security scans, whatever, that I'll get off of my soapbox the", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://share.transistor.fm/s/9d74230b#t=1962", "end": 2060.385, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "2911d2506f5ebbd15139b98e0e4438e8c668cacb250b1018d0f191a9aab55a47", "start": 1962.21, "text": "That's kind of principle one, and certainly things that people are are, addressing from a variety of angles. Thing two is these things are spawning so quickly. There there was likely no human that could have made decisions quick enough to r", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://share.transistor.fm/s/9d74230b#t=2322", "end": 2391.82, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "2da2e8fd6520b6f0deddce3f8517cdf6892b866433cd3524c160bad4206bea4e", "start": 2322.485, "text": "They were blocked because of the guardrails associated with that model, which they did not have control over. So they didn't control whether those guardrails were on or off. They were just uploading to the platform itself, which had an opin", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}], "current_topic": "Uncategorized", "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpts": [{"deep_link": "https://share.transistor.fm/s/9d74230b#t=1", "end": 75.865005, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "00d1f64b9e50371a6803968ceffc8af49777037930ad3b5d22b0df5dc16af29b", "start": 1.76, "text": "Welcome to the Practical AI Podcast, where we break down the real world applications of artificial intelligence and how it's shaping the way we live, work, and create. Our goal is to help make AI technology practical, productive, and access", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://share.transistor.fm/s/9d74230b#t=768", "end": 854.085, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "34b280631d8b09f8d5f0d90fc11fdf964e8d2a79a7ae5f