{"card_hash": "dbad26b53d1eabdf4408943fb4da03097dd99a866c3fa9f9884a845e9d6bdea5", "channel": "Latent Space: The AI Engineer Podcast", "chars": 77711, "chars_all_clips": 77711, "chars_chosen_clips": 1440, "clip_count": 64, "clips": [{"deep_link": "https://www.latent.space/p/chatgpt-work#t=99", "end": 152.94, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "52818700cdf5c4c80e0e9af6eb805086951cd8583e5fcee7191ee7817ce2d512", "start": 99.74, "text": "So chat GBT, codex app, chat GBT for work, have things changed? Actually, I think the more interesting thing is how things haven't changed. Like, I guess like one, I joined, I remember when I joined, it was like 500 people. One thing I was ", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://www.latent.space/p/chatgpt-work#t=984", "end": 1057.34, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "c82b5acac2a2872121274c6ce6cf8ec39b7713e5897138226e621669a926dfac", "start": 984.7, "text": "I think alongside that, outside of just harness and when they use Codex, HTTP tier work, there's also the new models you've released, right? Any guidance there. So people love to minmax what to use, like, only use Terra on high reasoning ve", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://www.latent.space/p/chatgpt-work#t=1239", "end": 1359.02, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "c8dad6cce04aa5ebd7c6ab93418c8af2a4cdadde48672f3d731946f2d07a3fa7", "start": 1239.9, "text": "Codex is still cooking. Yeah. And by the way, I, so I do know Gabriel Troye, he's part of the opening essay important. He showed me this. And I was like, pretty shocked that this looks like Excel. Edit Excel files. You never paid it in Exce", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://www.latent.space/p/chatgpt-work#t=2167", "end": 2261.66, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "46db8adc326867b10316b1d51f2acda3a32d8d46cb09280fc2e9de8f120c731d", "start": 2167.1, "text": "Do you have any power user advice? I feel like there's a group of people that will live it, use it for everything. Stay on it 24-7. And then there's a bit of a gap between that crew and people that, you know, okay, use it for work. I use it", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://www.latent.space/p/chatgpt-work#t=2640", "end": 2757.66, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "fe0fc5ee3c6828784cef6c5f05fbf1b4d73b310cfe5f4c90131508cf948e7b26", "start": 2640.62, "text": "If anything, it should increase the utility of something like Codex. Because now you can move seamlessly between writing a diff to creating an artifact or, you know, doing a search of your character. I do wonder how much this terminology le", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://www.latent.space/p/chatgpt-work#t=3438", "end": 3557.1, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "feac09a06d0320d4d52e831441c2aa7a9af6d841f12bf8b78aec7a65913f5862", "start": 3438.7, "text": "It's true that there are a lot of shorter sessions on chat, but I think the chat GPD, the product has had a ton of longevity, as long as this technology has been around, and people use it for working productivity-related things already toda", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}], "current_topic": "Uncategorized", "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpts": [{"deep_link": "https://www.latent.space/p/chatgpt-work#t=99", "end": 152.94, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "52818700cdf5c4c80e0e9af6eb805086951cd8583e5fcee7191ee7817ce2d512", "start": 99.74, "text": "So chat GBT, codex app, chat GBT for work, have things changed? Actually, I think the more interesting thing is how things haven't changed. Like, I guess like one, I joined, I remember when I joined, it was like 500 people. One thing I was ", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://www.latent.space/p/chatgpt-work#t=984", "end": 1057.34, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "c82b5acac2a2872121274c6ce